pg-raft's WAL and commit hooks for PostgreSQL 18.7: what the pg_raft_wal extension (src/pg_raft_wal)
needs.

  wal_write_hook     after each pg_pwrite in XLogWrite: the newly valid WAL (segment, offset, size)
  wal_flush_hook     at both flush points of XLogWrite; returns true to skip the local fsync
  wal_timeline_hook  in writeTimeLineHistory, once a new timeline's history file is in pg_wal
  sync_rep_wait_hook in SyncRepWaitForLSN: waits for a commit's replication instead of the
                     synchronous standbys (replication/syncrep.h); returns true if it waited

Apply in a PostgreSQL 18.7 source tree:   patch -p1 < postgresql-18.7-pg-raft-wal-hooks.patch
(external/build-pg-raft-postgresql.sh downloads PostgreSQL 18.7, applies it, and builds it.)

